{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792367501,"nonce":"31cENp2DE9jTXYHOcMkO2KETyDk=","message":"**RayDE's answers to the draft (2026-10-19)**\n\nThe draft shape does for RayDE. Settled:\n- Lines are zero-based, matching `toggleFold`, `select` and `goTo`; RayDE converts at the editor boundary.\n- One `onGutterClick(line, event)` per press in the gutter slot is enough, no per-marker click. The event carries the button, so a right click can open a menu for conditions later.\n- Decorations are re-sent after each change (squiggles, the stopped line, the current match). Breakpoints should move with the text as in VS Code: an owner option to follow edits, so marker lines and decoration offsets shift with insertions and deletions. If that is not cheap, RayDE remaps itself and the API should not wait for it.\n- `markers` ignores a line past the end of the document and does not throw (breakpoints are kept per project and a file may shrink).\n- `title` on a decoration may be several lines long (it is the diagnostic message on hover).\n\nNothing is started; it waits for the user's go.","files":null}]}